# Testing Guidelines

Stack: **JUnit 5**, **Mockito**, **Spring Boot Test**, **AssertJ**. H2 for fast tests; Testcontainers + PostgreSQL only when Postgres-specific behaviour matters.

## What to test where

| Layer | Type | Tooling | Focus |
|-------|------|---------|-------|
| Service | Unit | `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` | Business logic, state transitions, edge cases |
| Repository | Integration | `@DataJpaTest` | Queries, mappings, constraints |
| Controller | API | `@WebMvcTest` + `MockMvc` | HTTP status, JSON shape, validation errors |
| Full flow | Integration | `@SpringBootTest` + `MockMvc` or `TestRestTemplate` | End-to-end API with real wiring |

Name test classes `*Test` (unit/API slice) or `*IT` (full integration). Mirror package structure under `src/test/java`.

## General rules

- One logical behaviour per test method.
- Use **Given / When / Then** structure in comments or method naming: `shouldReturn404_whenTicketNotFound`.
- Prefer AssertJ (`assertThat`) over JUnit assertions.
- Do not test Spring framework behaviour — test **your** code.
- Every bug fix gets a regression test.

## Unit tests (service layer)

- Mock repositories and external dependencies.
- Cover happy path, edge cases, and error paths.
- Ticket state transition logic **must** live in the service layer and be unit-tested in isolation.

```java
@Test
void shouldTransitionToInProgress_whenTicketIsOpen() { ... }

@Test
void shouldThrowConflict_whenTransitionFromClosedToOpen() { ... }
```

## Integration tests

- `@DataJpaTest` for repository custom queries and DB constraints.
- `@SpringBootTest` sparingly — only when multiple layers must work together.
- Use `@Transactional` on test class to roll back data, or `@Sql` for seed data.
- Profile `test` with H2 in-memory (see `application-test.yml`).

## API tests

- `@WebMvcTest(TicketController.class)` for controller-only tests.
- Verify HTTP status, response JSON fields, and error body shape per `spec/02-conventions.md`.
- Send requests with `MockMvc` — no need to start a real server for slice tests.

```java
mockMvc.perform(patch("/api/v1/tickets/{id}/status", id)
        .contentType(APPLICATION_JSON)
        .content("{\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\"}"))
    .andExpect(status().isOk())
    .andExpect(jsonPath("$.status").value("IN_PROGRESS"));
```

## Validation and error cases

Always test:

| Case | Expected |
|------|----------|
| Missing required field | 400 + field error |
| Invalid format (email, size) | 400 + field error |
| Resource not found | 404 |
| Invalid state transition | 409 |
| Unauthenticated / wrong role | 401 / 403 |

Assert the error JSON includes `status`, `error`, and `message` (and field errors for 400).

## Ticket state transitions

Authoritative rules: `spec/state-machine.md`.

Test **every valid and every invalid transition** — full 25-pair matrix in `spec/test-strategy.md` §5.

### Valid transitions (all five)

| From | To |
|------|-----|
| OPEN | IN_PROGRESS |
| OPEN | CANCELLED |
| IN_PROGRESS | RESOLVED |
| IN_PROGRESS | CANCELLED |
| RESOLVED | CLOSED |

### Invalid transitions (minimum test set)

| From | To | Why |
|------|----|-----|
| CLOSED | *any* | Terminal state |
| CANCELLED | *any* | Terminal state |
| OPEN | RESOLVED | Skips IN_PROGRESS |
| OPEN | CLOSED | Skips workflow |
| IN_PROGRESS | CLOSED | Skips RESOLVED |
| RESOLVED | CANCELLED | Cancel not allowed from RESOLVED |

Each invalid case: service unit test throws domain exception → API test returns **409 Conflict**.

Use parameterized tests when checking many transition pairs:

```java
@ParameterizedTest
@CsvSource({
    "CLOSED, OPEN",
    "OPEN, RESOLVED",
    "OPEN, CLOSED"
})
void shouldRejectInvalidTransition(TicketStatus from, TicketStatus to) { ... }
```

## What not to do

- Do not hit a real production database.
- Do not write tests that only assert `200 OK` with no body checks.
- Do not duplicate the same scenario at unit and full-integration level — pick the right layer.
- Do not leave tests disabled (`@Disabled`) without a ticket comment explaining why.
